=== accelerator-shortcut --help ===
Usage: accelerator-shortcut <COMMAND>

Commands:
  show        Show a story or an epic as JSON
  search      Search the base team's stories, rendering a JSON envelope
  create      Create a story or an epic from a work item or an explicit title
  update      Update a story's or an epic's fields
  comment     Comment on a story or an epic
  transition  Move a story to a named state of its workflow
  attach      Attach a link to a story
  init        Verify the token, list teams, or discover the workspace's workflows
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut show --help ===
Show a story or an epic as JSON

Usage: accelerator-shortcut show [OPTIONS] <REFERENCE>

Arguments:
  <REFERENCE>  `sc-<id>`, `epic-<id>`, or a story or epic URL in this workspace

Options:
      --comments <COMMENTS>  Include the most recent N comments
  -q, --quiet                Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help                 Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut search --help ===
Search the base team's stories, rendering a JSON envelope

Usage: accelerator-shortcut search [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --state <STATE>  A workflow state name
      --owner <OWNER>  A member's mention name
      --label <LABEL>  A label name
      --type <TYPE>    A story type (feature, bug, chore) or a local kind
      --text <TEXT>    A phrase the story's text holds
      --limit <LIMIT>  Print at most this many stories
  -q, --quiet          Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help           Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut create --help ===
Create a story or an epic from a work item or an explicit title

Usage: accelerator-shortcut create [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  A work-item file whose title, kind and body seed the entity

Options:
      --title <TITLE>          The story's title, when there is no work-item file
      --body-file <BODY_FILE>  A Markdown body file, when there is no work-item file
  -q, --quiet                  Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help                   Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut update --help ===
Update a story's or an epic's fields

Usage: accelerator-shortcut update [OPTIONS] <REFERENCE>

Arguments:
  <REFERENCE>  `sc-<id>`, `epic-<id>`, or a story or epic URL in this workspace

Options:
      --title <TITLE>              
      --description <DESCRIPTION>  
      --state <STATE>              A state of the story's workflow. Stories only
      --owner <OWNER>              A member's mention name
      --estimate <ESTIMATE>        The story's points. Stories only
  -q, --quiet                      Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help                       Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut comment --help ===
Comment on a story or an epic

Usage: accelerator-shortcut comment <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add   Add a Markdown comment
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut comment add --help ===
Add a Markdown comment

Usage: accelerator-shortcut comment add [OPTIONS] <REFERENCE>

Arguments:
  <REFERENCE>  `sc-<id>`, `epic-<id>`, or a story or epic URL in this workspace

Options:
      --body <BODY>            
      --body-file <BODY_FILE>  
  -q, --quiet                  Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help                   Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut transition --help ===
Move a story to a named state of its workflow

Usage: accelerator-shortcut transition [OPTIONS] <REFERENCE> [STATE]

Arguments:
  <REFERENCE>  `sc-<id>`, or a story URL in this workspace
  [STATE]      The target state name, positional or as `--state`

Options:
      --state <STATE>  
  -q, --quiet          Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help           Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut attach --help ===
Attach a link to a story

Usage: accelerator-shortcut attach [OPTIONS] <REFERENCE>

Arguments:
  <REFERENCE>  `sc-<id>`, or a story URL in this workspace

Options:
      --url <URL>    An https URL to link
      --file <FILE>  Not supported yet: Shortcut file upload is not built
  -q, --quiet        Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help         Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init --help ===
Verify the token, list teams, or discover the workspace's workflows

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init <COMMAND>

Commands:
  verify      Verify the token without printing it
  list-teams  List the teams the token can see, by team key
  discover    Discover every team and workflow, and write catalogue.json
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init verify --help ===
Verify the token without printing it

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init verify [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -q, --quiet  Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help   Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init list-teams --help ===
List the teams the token can see, by team key

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init list-teams [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -q, --quiet  Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help   Print help

=== accelerator-shortcut init discover --help ===
Discover every team and workflow, and write catalogue.json

Usage: accelerator-shortcut init discover [OPTIONS] --team <TEAM>

Options:
      --team <TEAM>  The base team's key: its mention name
      --force        Replace a different `shortcut.team_key` already set
  -q, --quiet        Print no notices on stderr
  -h, --help         Print help

